# Support Workflow Process

## 1. Vendor Registration & Renewal
* Manage initial vendor registration and document intake.
* Collect legal, tax, order, and reference documents.
* Process ongoing registration renewals.

## 2. Inquiry & RFQ Intake
* Receive customer enquiries through primary channels: Email, GeM, or eProcurement portals.
* Circulate enquiries/RFQs to the relevant Profit Center Heads (PCH) and Technical Support Services (TSS).
* Download complete tender packages and document sets when receiving alerts via portals.

## 3. Estimation & Supplier Liaison
* Route technical and price queries to PCH and Procurement/Supply Chain Management (PSM).
* PSM coordinates with suppliers to gather pricing and estimates.
* Support receives final consolidated quotations back from PSM.

## 4. Tender Submission & Query Handling
* Upload structured quotations (PDF/Excel) and complete required form-filling on eProc or GeM portals using digital signatures.
* Coordinate with the finance team if Earnest Money Deposit (EMD) or bank guarantees are required.
* Address technical/commercial queries raised during tender evaluation by relaying details between customer, PCH, TSS, and PSM.
* Manage Reverse Auction (RA) price revisions on GeM if triggered.

## 5. Order Review & Order Confirmation (OC)
* Perform contract review upon receiving a Purchase Order (PO) to compare against original quotes and terms.
* Confirm validity and execution feasibility with PSM.
* Generate the Order Confirmation (OC) in the system once cleared.
* Issue Proforma Invoices (PI) via PCH if advance payment terms apply.

## 6. PO Placement & Delivery Scheduling
* PSM extracts OC data, places POs with suppliers, and retrieves confirmed delivery dates.
* Support updates delivery dates in the OC and communicates them to the customer via PCH.

## 7. Dispatch & Invoicing
* Upon receiving Goods Receipt Note (GRN) notification from logistics:
  * Cross-verify pending line items against the shipping plan.
  * Instruct logistics to prepare invoices after quality checks pass.
  * Coordinate dispatch to the customer.
